        "description":"Jezero Crater was selected as the exploration site for the Perseverance rover. Jezero's floor is rich in sedimentary deposits that accumulated on the crater floor when water once flowed across the surface of Mars. This ancient lakebed preserves clues about Mars' ancient environment, its possible past habitability, potential biomarkers preserved in sedimentary deposits, and changing geological processes over time. This tour takes a broad look at Jezero Crater, including locations not scheduled to be visited by Perseverance but helpful to understanding the importance of Jezero Crater and to providing context to the actual locations visited by Perseverance as shown in Mars Trek's Perseverance Landing Site bookmark.",
        "mediaType":["image"],
        "title":"Jezero Crater Features and Landforms",
